WEBVTT

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:15.950
Where are we?

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:59.130
<i>Is the shoot coming along well?</i>

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:00.260
Yes.

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:03.550
It's going to be a great special feature.

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:06.020
<i>It's B-Project's first fan book, too.</i>

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:10.020
<i>Tell the boys to make sure 
there's plenty of fan service.</i>

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:12.400
Got it.

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:16.720
Now then.

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:22.730
You won't beat me.

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:24.130
I accept your challenge.

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:37.090
Don't miss any spots.

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.520
I'll rub some on you, too, Momo.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:46.370
<i>(YOU) It's sad that we are</i>

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:45.310
I'm good.

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:47.060
There's no need to hold back.

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:49.310
<i>(FEEL) Such lonely creatures</i>

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:49.310
No, really.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:52.880
<i>(I) The farther we're apart, 
the more I'm drawn to you</i>

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:56.060
<i>(DO) Like a shattered magnet</i>

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:56.780
Take this!

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:57.810
<i>Say Never look it back</i>

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:58.150
Ashu and Osa...

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.570
<i>Don't stop</i>

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:00.460
Splash!

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:01.040
<i>We're just moving on</i>

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:02.600
<i>Keep on searching</i>

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:02.600
You got me.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:05.120
<i>With this hope</i>

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:05.930
Do it, Nome.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:09.140
<i>And the strength to get 
up time and time again</i>

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:11.250
<i>The wings I spread</i>

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:14.740
<i>Will lead me far away</i>

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:21.220
<i>Towards the light</i>

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:22.300
<i>So</i>

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:29.110
<i>Like a beat that changes everything</i>

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:30.770
Okay! Let's head to the next location!

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:35.170
<i>Is this resonance reaching you?</i>

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:38.330
There's sunscreen and towels in the bag 
and some light snacks in the cooler.

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:42.330
<i>The harmony of an adventurer 
that changes everything</i>

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:40.690
Thanks for everything, Tsubasa.

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:43.700
Have fun, guys!

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:52.710
<i>Never fading, always leading towards 
a miracle is Kodo Ambitious!</i>

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:10.640
Looks like rain.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:15.480
Let's stop filming!

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:20.230
Oh, no! We're being swept away!

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:23.090
Captain! Can we get onto the other cruiser?

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:24.240
Don't be ridiculous!

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:25.160
What?

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:29.130
They're already so far away.

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:30.770
Get inside! Quickly!

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:32.970
Wait! B-Pro is...

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:34.540
Sumisora-san, hurry!

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:37.290
G-Guys!

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:47.900
After that, everything 
got mixed up in the storm.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:49.970
And we arrived at this beach.

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:52.220
I'm glad we weren't washed out to sea.

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:55.700
I hope Tsubasa and the others are all right.

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:56.730
Yeah.

00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:00.230
Wait. Where are we, anyway?

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:05.090
It doesn't look like 
the island we were on earlier.

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:07.360
Could this be a deserted island?

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:09.040
A deserted island?

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:12.330
I can't believe we're in a situation 
straight out of a comic book.

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:16.830
You're enjoying this situation, 
aren't you, Mika and Ashu?

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:18.410
Yeah, well...

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:21.590
I don't believe it.

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:24.340
Aren't you worried that 
we might be stuck here?

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:25.830
Not at all.

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:29.780
After all, we have these fantastic 
devices known as cell phones.

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:30.730
Right?

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:31.970
Oh, right. Our phones.

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:33.340
Does anyone have theirs?

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:39.340
Of course not. Who would have 
their phone on them during a shoot?

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:41.360
Actually, I have mine.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:42.860
Nice, Ai-chan.

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:46.260
I always carry mine around 
in case a girl calls me.

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:49.930
You shouldn't be doing that as an idol, 
but you saved us this time.

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:52.240
Kento, let's call Tsubasa.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.450
Okay.

00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:58.750
<i>Aizome-san? Are you all right?</i>

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.250
Tsubasa!

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.250
Tsubasa-chan!

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:02.430
You're all okay.

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:04.000
<i>Yeah, everyone's fine.</i>

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:07.140
That's great. So, where are you right now?

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:10.570
The call ended.

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:15.850
It's no use. It can't complete the call.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:18.310
Could it be because it's wet?

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:20.980
I don't know. There's no signal, either.

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:22.360
<b>Sumisora Tsubasa</b>

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:25.280
We found a map.

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:28.900
This is the area where we were shooting.

00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:34.660
Based on the direction of the wind and current, 
they probably washed up around here.

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:36.950
On one of these islands?

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:42.230
Their phone picked up a signal, so let's 
search the islands that have cell signals.

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:43.480
They must be on one of them.

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:47.020
I'm going to call the office.

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:50.930
We were able to tell them we're okay.

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:53.640
Someone will probably come to rescue us soon.

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:57.560
Then we shouldn't move around too much.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:11.030
I'm hungry.

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:14.460
Waiting for help is good and all,

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:17.480
but won't it be bad if night
falls while we're still here?

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:19.040
I'm hungry!

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:24.190
Hey, someone! I'm going to starve to death!

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:26.670
Hey, Hikaru.

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:27.830
Isn't that...

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:29.170
What?

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:34.690
Tsubasa-chan's cooler!

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:37.180
Food supplies secured!

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:48.060
What was that?

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:51.070
That wasn't a human voice.

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:55.350
Hey, don't tell me it's a ghost again.

00:07:55.350 --> 00:07:57.110
Maybe it's an animal.

00:07:57.110 --> 00:07:58.470
Like a bear?

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:00.010
Perhaps it's a dinosaur.

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:03.080
Quit making things up!

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:08.840
Before it gets dark, we should 
secure shelter and make a fire.

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:11.840
B-Project is lost at sea?

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:13.840
What do you mean?

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:16.300
This is an important time for them.

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:18.940
If anything happens to them...

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:20.520
<i>I promise we'll find them.</i>

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:22.850
Aw, jeez!

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:25.480
I can't believe there's 
nothing I can do right now.

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:28.020
I'm counting on you, Tsubasa-chan.

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:34.990
These bananas are delicious.

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:36.450
Delicious bananas!

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:41.040
If Yuta hadn't been so clumsy, 
we could've gotten a lot more.

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:43.460
Bananas!

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:46.710
There's rice, too. Hooray! Hooray!

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:51.350
Whoa!

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.470
I'm sorry.

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:04.430
You're always clumsy.

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:07.690
He's right. I'm glad 
that's all that happened.

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:14.900
We found the cruiser's survival kit, too.

00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:17.900
It's a good thing no water got inside.

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:21.330
This is one of those radios you 
power by turning the crank, right?

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:24.080
I don't hear anything, though.

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:28.210
Like the phone, it's probably 
not picking up a signal.

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:29.330
I see.

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:33.700
Anyway, should we be 
this deep inside the forest?

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:35.110
That voice we heard earlier—

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:39.360
Don't worry, Kaneshiro. 
That wasn't a person or a ghost.

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:41.890
Really?

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:44.320
I was thinking about this the other day,

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:48.120
but it's cute how 
easily scared you are, Kane-san.

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:49.750
I'm not scared, stupid!

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:55.030
What is it?

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:57.530
Look. Mulberries.

00:09:57.530 --> 00:09:59.660
Don't scare me like that.

00:09:59.920 --> 00:10:02.660
Mulberries? I'm surprised 
you knew what they were.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:04.330
Of course I do.

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:08.370
In episode 68 of <i>Witch Girl Mamirin</i>, 
"Girl's Fruit Detox,"

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:13.170
these berries, also known as 
heart berries, saved Mamirin!

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:15.080
What is he talking about?

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:16.290
Who knows?

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:18.880
Kaneshiro, above you.

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:19.830
What?

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:21.640
They're green papayas.

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:25.350
They look delicious.

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:28.230
If you remove the harshness from them 
with water, you can eat them raw.

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:30.700
Nomecchi, you know a lot about plants, too?

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:31.970
No, not really.

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:36.530
I just realized how useless I am after 
the mugwort incident the other day.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:38.530
I did some research.

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:42.900
Really? That's amazing, Nomecchi.

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:48.040
What is it this time?

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:50.090
I found a cave!

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:53.030
There was a radio on the cruiser?

00:10:53.030 --> 00:10:54.570
An emergency one.

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:57.440
If it wasn't thrown overboard, 
they should be able to use it.

00:10:58.020 --> 00:11:01.010
I don't think we can start 
searching for them right now.

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:02.790
No...

00:11:03.270 --> 00:11:05.490
<i>I can't believe all we can do is wait.</i>

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:11.190
We know they're all right, so we're 
waiting until morning to search for them.

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:17.020
How many radio stations does the island have?

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:18.070
Radio stations?

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:19.440
Yes.

00:11:20.190 --> 00:11:23.640
<i>Even if we can't go look for them, 
there must be something we can do.</i>

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:28.830
Isn't it great? 
Now we'll be fine even if it rains.

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:32.080
Do you think it's possible 
that dinosaurs live in here?

00:11:32.340 --> 00:11:37.090
There must be dinosaurs that escaped 
extinction living here on this island!

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:41.340
Or maybe it's the nest of giant insects 
that evolved here independently.

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:42.640
I-Insects?

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:44.720
I-I don't like bugs.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:46.160
Ba-dump!

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:49.470
The members of THRIVE are just too cute.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:52.710
You mentioned bugs intentionally, 
didn't you, Momo?

00:11:53.220 --> 00:11:54.480
Intentionally?

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:59.360
It means you did something 
a little bit mean on purpose.

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:01.790
That's not what I was asking.

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:02.610
Oh?

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:05.990
What you just did is what you 
call intentional, Sekimura.

00:12:11.050 --> 00:12:13.710
Well? Does it seem safe?

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:18.330
Let's split up into groups.

00:12:18.330 --> 00:12:25.330
Ryuji, Yuta, Goshi, Kento, and 
Tomohisa, could you gather firewood?

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:28.980
The rest of you come 
with me and explore this cave.

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:33.960
Question! Can Tatsu and I look for more food?

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:35.980
That's fine. Be careful.

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:38.190
Do you need my knowledge?

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:39.970
Nah, we don't need you.

00:12:39.970 --> 00:12:41.210
We've got Tatsu.

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:43.860
Mika, let's go.

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:49.050
Be careful, everyone.

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:52.830
Make sure you come back alive.

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:56.210
Wait. Eh? Huh?

00:12:57.130 --> 00:13:00.000
Is this that serious?

00:13:07.650 --> 00:13:08.470
Yuta.

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:11.930
Hey, Yuta.

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:15.390
Yuta!

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:18.680
What is it, Ryu-chan?

00:13:18.680 --> 00:13:21.430
There's no one behind us.

00:13:21.430 --> 00:13:22.090
What?

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:28.790
Did we get separated?

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:32.390
I was stupid for following you.

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:37.140
Sorry.

00:13:41.970 --> 00:13:45.610
I really am useless.

00:13:45.610 --> 00:13:46.420
What?

00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:50.100
I ruined the food we found.

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:53.040
And unlike Mikarin and Nomecchi, 
I don't know anything.

00:13:53.470 --> 00:14:00.030
On top of that, when you had amnesia, 
I couldn't do anything for you.

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:03.790
I couldn't heroically 
save you like Tomo-kun did.

00:14:05.230 --> 00:14:06.620
What's gotten into you?

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:09.820
There's no way you could 
ever be cooler than Tomo.

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:17.560
You're right. Considering how 
clumsy I am, it's only natural.

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:19.210
That's not what I meant.

00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:22.460
That's not what I'm trying to say.

00:14:24.100 --> 00:14:26.400
You and Tomo are different people.

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:31.850
There are things Tomo can't do 
that you can do, and vice versa.

00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:35.850
Though I wouldn't be happy 
unless you're both around.

00:14:37.230 --> 00:14:40.360
There are things the 
perfect Tomo-kun can't do?

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:42.080
Like what?

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:43.980
Who knows?

00:14:44.260 --> 00:14:46.410
Use your head.

00:14:49.870 --> 00:14:53.160
I know. Like getting along with Massu?

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:58.290
Tomo and Kazu, huh? You're right.

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:01.480
But those two...

00:15:07.530 --> 00:15:08.800
All right!

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:17.050
This is harder work than I thought.

00:15:17.050 --> 00:15:19.230
This should be enough.

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:21.240
Huh? Where are Ryu and Yuta?

00:15:21.240 --> 00:15:22.020
What?

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:26.520
This isn't good. Yuta's poor sense 
of direction must've gotten them lost.

00:15:27.210 --> 00:15:28.370
Those idiots...

00:15:32.620 --> 00:15:35.580
Something tapped the back of my neck!

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:37.390
They touched it!

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:39.400
Are you sure it wasn't just a drop of water?

00:15:39.400 --> 00:15:41.780
What? Oh. Oh...

00:15:41.780 --> 00:15:44.210
That's all it was?

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:49.300
Where's Kazu?

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:52.720
Oh, no. He's still inside the cave.

00:16:06.580 --> 00:16:07.480
Kazu!

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:12.400
Tomohisa?

00:16:13.710 --> 00:16:20.530
<i>Always hiding my real face</i>

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:22.290
Good. You have light.

00:16:20.530 --> 00:16:28.750
<i>I maintain the smiling face of a liar</i>

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:24.900
What? What's wrong?

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:27.850
The other two came running out of the cave.

00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:30.880
I thought it might be pitch black inside.

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:35.970
<i>In your eyes do I appear as a Liar?</i>

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:35.970
I'll be fine on my own.

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:37.720
I'll come back once I'm done investigating.

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:44.600
<i>Before you, I'm not okay with it</i>

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:40.810
You can't. It's dangerous.

00:16:42.470 --> 00:16:43.270
Kazu?

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:46.450
I want to be alone.

00:16:45.030 --> 00:16:54.350
<i>In this monochrome world 
even though no one else knows</i>

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:48.720
What? Kazu!

00:16:50.680 --> 00:16:51.230
Kazu!

00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:52.910
Wait! Stop!

00:16:52.910 --> 00:16:54.350
Why are you following me?

00:16:54.350 --> 00:17:00.940
<i>Why are you the only one 
who can see through me?</i>

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:07.200
You're always casually standing in front 
of me and shining brighter than anyone.

00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:09.670
<i>Suddenly your paint blends 
into the colors in my heart</i>

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:09.670
Tomohisa, as long as I'm with you...

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:16.910
<i>Stop the time for a minute 
without touching you</i>

00:17:11.220 --> 00:17:13.680
My mom will never find me.

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:15.420
Kazu...

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:20.390
I've worked hard to become 
a top idol so my mom,

00:17:16.910 --> 00:17:24.780
<i>The color of heart with you</i>

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:21.940
who's out there somewhere, 
might find me eventually.

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:26.440
But you're always standing in front of me.

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:31.630
I look so dim compared to your light.

00:17:34.640 --> 00:17:39.390
I see. You don't realize how bright you are.

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:41.950
What?

00:17:42.590 --> 00:17:47.760
Just as you see me, you appear 
blindingly bright to me

00:17:48.760 --> 00:17:52.760
as you attempt to take steps 
forward, Masunaga Kazuna.

00:17:55.400 --> 00:18:02.470
But through some miracle, we're not 
Kitakore or MooNs, or Kitakado or Masunaga.

00:18:03.070 --> 00:18:04.220
We're B-Project.

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:12.110
The brightness of two or even ten reaches 
much farther than the brightness of one.

00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:15.490
I saw it then.

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:20.120
B-Pro's music illuminated the world.

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:24.760
Don't you think that 
brightness and those voices

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:29.120
would knock on anyone's heart, 
no matter where they are?

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:32.760
Even your mother's.

00:18:51.750 --> 00:18:53.540
You heard those voices, too, right?

00:18:56.550 --> 00:18:57.270
Ryuji?

00:18:57.270 --> 00:18:58.160
Tomo?

00:18:58.800 --> 00:19:00.410
Oh, good.

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:02.550
Why are you here? 
Where did you come from?

00:19:02.550 --> 00:19:05.630
We found another cave, so we went inside.

00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:08.820
What's wrong, Massu?

00:19:08.820 --> 00:19:09.500
Huh?

00:19:13.070 --> 00:19:13.960
Were you crying?

00:19:14.870 --> 00:19:16.350
I-I wasn't crying!

00:19:20.310 --> 00:19:21.590
Hey, guess what?

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:24.300
We found an incredible place over there.

00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:25.970
An incredible place?

00:19:29.630 --> 00:19:31.560
What an amazing view of the stars!

00:19:32.110 --> 00:19:35.060
I wasn't expecting a place 
like this inside a cave.

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:41.180
What's this?

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:46.450
<i>Your pounding beat is everything</i>

00:19:44.070 --> 00:19:45.580
That's "Eternal Paradise."

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:50.820
<i>Inside my heart is</i>

00:19:47.840 --> 00:19:50.820
I can't believe we can even 
listen to B-Pro's songs here.

00:19:50.820 --> 00:19:54.330
<i>An eternal paradise</i>

00:19:50.820 --> 00:19:54.330
Is this the miracle of B-Pro 
you mentioned, Tomohisa?

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:57.760
<i>It's paradise</i>

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:57.760
The stars are like concert lights.

00:19:57.760 --> 00:19:59.510
<i>You can fly! You can fly!</i>

00:19:59.510 --> 00:20:01.000
<i>More and more</i>

00:19:59.950 --> 00:20:03.490
I bet the Japan Dome's 
stage is like this, too.

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:02.610
<i>You can fire! You can fire!</i>

00:20:02.610 --> 00:20:04.340
<i>Feel it together</i>

00:20:03.490 --> 00:20:05.010
Yeah, probably.

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:05.680
<i>You can fly! You can fly!</i>

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:07.370
<i>Deep inside</i>

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:07.850
I wish we could perform at the Dome.

00:20:07.370 --> 00:20:13.720
<i>Keep going for it 
Oh, yeah</i>

00:20:08.510 --> 00:20:09.570
Yeah.

00:20:09.570 --> 00:20:10.510
Let's do it.

00:20:10.510 --> 00:20:11.330
Yeah.

00:20:13.720 --> 00:20:17.920
<i>Due to a change of plans, tonight 
we're bringing you a B-Pro special.</i>

00:20:17.920 --> 00:20:21.360
<i>Are their passionate feelings reaching you?</i>

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:26.320
<i>We've got loads of songs 
recommended by B-Pro's A&R coming up.</i>

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:29.470
<i>Next up is "The Power of Dreaming" by MooNs.</i>

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:29.470
B-Pro's A&R?

00:20:29.470 --> 00:20:30.660
Tsubasa-chan?

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:40.430
Apparently, our A&R is capable of miracles, too.

00:20:42.030 --> 00:20:44.560
<i>Can you guys hear the music?</i>

00:20:45.190 --> 00:20:48.130
<i>This is all I can do for you right now.</i>

00:20:48.130 --> 00:20:50.770
<i>But no matter what happens, don't give up.</i>

00:20:53.780 --> 00:20:56.440
It's our turn to create a miracle.

00:20:57.650 --> 00:20:59.600
Open your eyes, B-Pro.

00:21:00.020 --> 00:21:01.760
This isn't our Dome.

00:21:02.170 --> 00:21:05.410
Let's make our performance 
at the Japan Dome a reality!

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:07.160
Yeah!

00:21:09.820 --> 00:21:10.850
Is that...

00:21:15.310 --> 00:21:17.670
Is this really the right way?

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:20.170
Yeah. It should be in this direction.

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:26.220
A radio tower?

00:21:26.220 --> 00:21:27.720
<b>Under Construction</b>

00:21:32.920 --> 00:21:34.140
Look. Over there.

00:21:37.550 --> 00:21:41.460
So this is the true identity 
of the mysterious groaning.

00:21:43.760 --> 00:21:44.980
This is...

00:21:45.840 --> 00:21:47.540
one of our research facilities.

00:21:49.390 --> 00:21:50.580
What?

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:51.580
<b>Kitakado Pharmaceuticals Research Facility</b>

00:21:52.760 --> 00:21:55.440
What?!

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:56.670
The Kitakado family is filthy rich!

00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:32.300
All members of B-Pro are safe and sound.

00:23:32.300 --> 00:23:34.380
<i>That's a relief.</i>

00:23:38.800 --> 00:23:41.320
<i>Oh, please. Are you crying, Tsubasa-chan?</i>

00:23:41.320 --> 00:23:42.350
Well...

00:23:43.850 --> 00:23:45.020
<i>You dummy.</i>

00:23:50.080 --> 00:23:51.740
I understand.

00:23:52.750 --> 00:23:54.200
Thank you.

00:23:54.990 --> 00:24:01.000
<b>A Cheating PLAY BOY</b>

00:23:55.770 --> 00:23:58.860
Where do you want your good morning kiss?
